<article class="env-lemma" id="02FL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02FL">Lemma <span data-tag="02FL">10.151.4</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map. If $R \to S$ is unramified, then there exists an idempotent $e \in S \otimes _ R S$ such that $S \otimes _ R S \to S$ is isomorphic to $S \otimes _ R S \to (S \otimes _ R S)_ e$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $J = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(S \otimes _ R S \to S)$. By assumption $J/J^2 = 0$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00RW" data-tag="00RW">10.131.13</a>. Since $S$ is of finite type over $R$ we see that $J$ is finitely generated, namely by $x_ i \otimes 1 - 1 \otimes x_ i$, where $x_ i$ generate $S$ over $R$. We win by Lemma <a href="/tag/00EH" data-tag="00EH">10.21.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>